invariant: INV-16
file: p256_sign.c
catches: hash_runtime_test
reason: p256_sign_cpu hands its nonce generator 0 in place of the
  session's ch_cfg.cpu, so a server that stated the SHA-256 instructions
  runs the sixteen HMAC-SHA-256 calls of every signature's RFC 6979 nonce
  on the portable code (docs/decisions.md 102). Every signature is the
  same, because both paths compute the same HMAC, so no vector fails.
  bin/hash_runtime_test counts the calls p256_sign_cpu makes into each
  path under every ch_cfg.cpu value.

--- old
    return sign_digest(widemul_of_cpu(cpu), cpu, priv, msg_hash, sig, cap, sig_len);
--- new
    return sign_digest(widemul_of_cpu(cpu), 0, priv, msg_hash, sig, cap, sig_len);
